  "style": {
    "address": "Harry and Cybil: Sie in the cafe (map0_s01), du from the antique shop on (map4_s01, map6_s01, map6_s04). Harry and Lisa: du from the first line. Harry and Kaufmann: Sie, both ways. Dahlia to everyone: du, elevated and archaic (vermag, ehe, eile, Finsternis); Harry to Dahlia: Sie until the amusement park, du in the last scene (map7_s03). Dahlia and Kaufmann: du. Harry to Alessa: du. Alessa to Dahlia: Mama, Mami; Dahlia of herself to Alessa: Mami. Cheryl to Harry: Papa. The UFO ending addresses the aliens with ihr.",
    "gender": "German verbs do not carry the speaker's gender; nouns do: Polizistin (Cybil), die Einzige (Lisa), der Einzige (Harry), Patientin (Alessa in Lisa's diary), Diebin (the graffiti addressed to Alessa). The demon is 'er/ihn', the God of the cult 'Er/Seiner' capitalised.",
    "quotes": "„ “ for the [ ] of the English; the dash is the character — (U+2014), which the English writes as '='. Three dots stay three ASCII dots.",
    "item_in_sentence": "an item name inside a sentence stands without an article, so no case or gender is needed: '<name> gefunden. Mitnehmen?', '<name> benutzt.', '<name> erhalten.'",
    "floors": "floors are named so that they match the in-game maps whatever the reader's convention: Erdgeschoss, Obergeschoss, 2. Untergeschoss; room numbers stay (Zimmer 201).",
    "units": "inches and feet are converted (25 bis 40 cm, 1 m); the clock times of the puzzle stay 10:00, 12:00, 5:00.",
    "spelling": "reformed spelling with ß (dass, muss, Straße, heißen); capital ß is not used: WEISSE CLAUDIA."
  },
